            <ArticleTitle>Left main coronary angioplasty in a 10-year-old boy with homozygous familial hypercholesterolemia.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>24-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Homozygous familial hypercholesterolemia is a rare cause of premature coronary artery disease. A young boy with this disorder who underwent successful coronary angioplasty for left main stem stenosis is presented.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
